/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 1pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 53.3pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 1pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 1pt; border-top: 2.25pt double rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); padding-top: 1pt"&gt; 							&lt;span style="font-size: 4pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 				&lt;/tr&gt; 			&lt;/table&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin: 4.6pt 0.9pt 6pt 27.35pt; line-height: 102%"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The reported effective tax rates of 26.9% for 2025 and 28.2% for 2024 differ from the U.S. federal statutory tax rate of 21% primarily due to state income taxes and the regulatory treatment of the equity portion of the AFUDC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;The reconciliation of taxes computed at the statutory federal income tax rate to the income tax provision is as follows (in thousands):&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width: 460.7pt; margin-left: 21.8pt; border-collapse: collapse" class="e-rte-table"&gt; 				&lt;tr style="height: 12.6pt"&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 264.05pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 4.3pt; margin-bottom: 0.5pt; text-indent: -4.3pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid"&gt; 							&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 						&lt;/p&gt; 					&lt;/td&gt; 					&lt;td style="width: 53.3pt; padding-right: 5.4pt; padding-left: 5.4pt; vertical-align: bottom"&gt; 						&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: center; pag