        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1087_334471_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; display: inline !important; float: none">Revenue earned from PJM per the revenue requirement for transmission services filed with FERC.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1328_334472_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; display: inline !important; float: none">The Capacity of the Substation is based the Emergency Rating of the submarine cable between Silver Run and Hope Creek. There are other lines that connect to Silver Run which are owned by other Transmission Owner that have lower Emergency Ratings.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
    </link:footnoteLink>
</xbrl>